4364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,32,23739,315,3108,220,18,14924,702,264,23739,315,3108,220,16,17122,3931,504,1817,9131,13,362,23739,315,3108,220,17,14924,374,1221,21578,304,1817,9131,13,3555,374,279,1372,315,9334,14924,304,279,7329,3082,315,279,12942,6437,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA cube of side 3 inches has a cube of side 1 inch cut from each corner. A cube of side 2 inches is then inserted in each corner. What is the number of square inches in the surface area of the resulting solid?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"73ad80949f0efd118fbf2a7fbf78077d4c5668835efe6b443b70697223d23658"},"seconds":38.204575061798096,"seed":904028114380315200,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the surface area of the resulting solid after the described modifications, we will follow a step-by-step approach.\n\n### Initial Cube Surface Area\n\n1. **Calculate the surface area of the original cube:**\n   - The side length of the original cube is \\(3\\) inches.\n   - The surface area of a cube is given by \\(6 \\times (\\text{side length})^2\\).\n   \\[\n   \\text{Initial surface area} = 6 \\times 3^2 = 6 \\times 9 = 54 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n### Cutting Out Smaller Cubes\n\n2. **Determine the effect of cutting out smaller cubes:**\n   - A cube of side \\(1\\) inch is cut from each corner. There are \\(8\\) corners.\n   - Each cut-out removes a \\(1 \\times 1 \\times 1\\) cube which exposes \\(3\\) new \\(1 \\times 1\\) faces (one for each dimension).\n   - Total new faces exposed by all 8 corners:\n   \\[\n   8 \\times 3 = 24 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   - Each face added is \\(1 \\times 1 = 1\\) square inch.\n\n### Inserting Larger Cubes\n\n3. **Determine the effect of inserting larger cubes:**\n   - A cube of side \\(2\\) inches is inserted in each corner.\n   - Each inserted cube obscures \\(3\\) of the \\(1 \\times 1\\) faces that were exposed by the cut-out.\n   - Total faces obscured by the inserted cubes:\n   \\[\n   8 \\times 3 = 24 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   - Each face added by the inserted cube is \\(2 \\times 2 = 4\\) square inches, and each corner has \\(3\\) such faces.\n   - Total new faces added by all 8 corners:\n   \\[\n   8 \\times 3 \\times 4 = 96 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n### Recalculate the Surface Area\n\n4. **Calculate the new surface area:**\n   - Start with the initial surface area:\n   \\[\n   54 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   - Add the new faces exposed by the cut-outs:\n   \\[\n   54 + 24 = 78 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   - Subtract the faces obscured by the inserted cubes (since they were already counted in the exposed faces):\n   \\[\n   78 - 24 = 54 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   - Add the new faces from the larger cubes:\n   \\[\n   54 + 96 = 150 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\nThe number of square inches in the surface area of the resulting solid is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{150}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{150}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
